The revised milestones address my earlier concern. With `max_distance=5`:

- **Player spawns at (0,0,0)** relative, pillar is at **(8,2,8)** — distance ≈ 11.5 blocks
- Player must walk **at least ~6.5 blocks closer** before the "find" milestone triggers
- This is reasonable — at 5 blocks distance, the player is clearly standing next to the structure
- The terracotta mound extends from (6,-1,6) to (11,-1,11), so the player will be standing on or right next to the terracotta when the "find" milestone triggers — perfect setup for the "mine" task

